{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C5-noop-commit-reproposes-admitted-operation\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"bounded_liveness\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"When a replica that owns an instance and still holds an admitted client operation for it receives a commit carrying a single NONE command for that instance, the replica must install the commit and re-propose the pending operation onto its propose path, so the admitted operation is not silently dropped.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S25-defs-channels\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Owner-alive case: one replica owns instance (0,0), admitted one client operation for it, and receives one legal single-NONE Commit for that instance.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the owner's record still holds its leader bookkeeping and the admitted proposal\\\",\\\"the commit is well formed for that instance\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"the restarted-owner case, where the record has no bookkeeping (claim C4 covers the crash there)\\\",\\\"the client library's own retry behaviour\\\",\\\"execution of the re-proposed operation and its reply\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"handlePropose attaches the admitted GPropose to the instance bookkeeping, and handleCommit's NOOP branch for the replica's own row pushes those proposals back onto ProposeChan and clears them, which is the only path that keeps an admitted operation alive across a NOOP commit.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Owner-alive case of a NOOP recovery; the client-facing reply still depends on the re-proposed operation being committed and executed.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the restarted-owner case is a separate claim\\\",\\\"the client's own retry behaviour is outside this check\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb6={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB6-repropose\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handleCommit\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1066,\\\"end_line\\\":1113,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Commit installation and the NOOP branch that re-proposes the owner's pending client proposals onto ProposeChan.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C5-noop-commit-reproposes-admitted-operation\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The branch is the mechanism the claim asserts: it iterates the instance's clientProposals, writes each back to ProposeChan and clears the list.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: in the owner-alive case, does a legal single-NONE Commit for the owner's instance leave the admitted operation pending nowhere, or is it re-proposed onto the propose channel? Prefix: the harness admits the operation with the real handlePropose (which attaches it and broadcasts the PreAccept) and then delivers the commit to the real handleCommit. Controls: the same events print whether bookkeeping and a pending proposal existed before the commit, the instance status after it, the remaining pending count and the number of proposals on the channel.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that admits one proposal with the real handler and delivers one legal NOOP commit, reporting the pending counts and the propose channel.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: the Replica is constructed in-package with buffer peer writers and the two handlers are called directly; the handlers are unmodified\\\",\\\"the commit is delivered directly instead of through the run loop, so only the handler's effect on the proposal is observed\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admitted_proposal\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"proposal_admitted\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"has_bookkeeping\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"Both steps are the protocol's own: handlePropose is what admits a client operation and the commit is what a recoverer broadcasts for a NOOP instance.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"One instance, one admitted operation, one commit.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the run loop's later handling of the re-proposed proposal is not driven\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-repropose\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-repropose\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"noop_commit_at_owner\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports the instance status after the commit, the remaining pending proposals and the proposals waiting on the channel, which together say whether the operation was re-proposed.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The owner held the admitted proposal and the commit was for its own instance.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"admitted_proposal.instance\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admitted_proposal\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-repropose\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"noop_commit_at_owner\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"reproposed_on_channel\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After the owner processes a NOOP commit for an instance holding its admitted operation, the operation must be waiting on the propose channel.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check covers the owner-alive case only; the restarted-owner case is claim C4's crash\\\",\\\"the later commit and execution of the re-proposed operation are not driven, so the client's reply is not observed\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":6,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"In the owner-alive case, when a replica that admitted a client operation for instance (0,0) receives a legal single-NONE Commit for that instance, does it install the commit and put the operation back on its propose path, or does the admitted operation remain dropped?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"The NOOP re-proposal path is the only mechanism in the snapshot that keeps an admitted operation alive when its instance is committed as NOOP, so whether it fires decides whether the client's operation is retried inside the replica or lost. Establishing it as a protection also delimits the crash recorded in claim C4, which is the same handler with the bookkeeping absent.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S25-defs-channels\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S6-conflicts-watermarks\\\",\\\"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S9-handlePreAccept\\\",\\\"S7-attributes\\\",\\\"S21-quorum-sizes\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"owner-alive case: the instance's bookkeeping still holds the admitted proposal\\\",\\\"commit carrying a single NONE command for the owner's instance\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"handlePropose admits the operation and attaches it to the instance\\\",\\\"a recoverer commits the instance as NOOP\\\",\\\"the owner's handleCommit processes the commit\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A1\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B1-admit-propose\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F5-pending-proposal\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B6-commit-install\\\":\\\"the handler that contains the re-proposal branch\\\",\\\"B16-client-reply\\\":\\\"the consumer that eventually answers the re-proposed operation\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"preservation\\\",\\\"priority\\\":2,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: the branch requires commit.Replica == r.Id, a single NONE command and non-nil clientProposals, and it writes each proposal back to ProposeChan before clearing the list (S13-handleCommit)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the harness: the local construction run with bookkeeping present reports instance_status COMMITTED, pending_after 0 and reproposed_on_channel 1\\\"],\n \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"whether the re-proposed operation's later commit and execution complete the client's reply, which is not driven here\\\",\\\"the restarted-owner case with no bookkeeping is claim C4's crash and is excluded\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"The A1 relationship is the admission of the client operation into decision formation: B1-admit-propose establishes the pending-proposal fact, and the question asks whether that fact survives a NOOP commit by being re-admitted through the same path, which is the protection the client contract depends on.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"First check for the owner-alive half of the client-completion question, which also delimits the confirmed crash in claim C4: with the admitted proposal still in the instance's bookkeeping, a legal NOOP commit installs the instance and re-proposes the operation onto the propose channel. The harness admits the operation with the real handlePropose and delivers the commit to the real handleCommit, and the local construction run reports COMMITTED with pending_after 0 and reproposed_on_channel 1; the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome, which is expected to hold.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-repropose.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_repropose_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; this is the protection that keeps an admitted operation alive across a NOOP commit and the counterpart of the C4 crash for the same handler.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b6]}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-repropose.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-repropose.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-repropose.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
